{"type":"standard","title":"James W. Byrd","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">James W. Byrd</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16186169","titles":{"canonical":"James_W._Byrd","normalized":"James W. Byrd","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">James W. Byrd</span></span>"},"pageid":23126737,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/James_W._Byrd_at_Campbell_County_League_of_Women_Voters%27_General_Election_Candidates%27_Forum_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-James_W._Byrd_at_Campbell_County_League_of_Women_Voters%27_General_Election_Candidates%27_Forum_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":439},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/James_W._Byrd_at_Campbell_County_League_of_Women_Voters%27_General_Election_Candidates%27_Forum_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":1596,"height":2125},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1371279773","tid":"1acd3cf7-a0a2-11f1-8b91-852b1e14d741","timestamp":"2026-08-25T16:29:12Z","description":"American politician (born 1954)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_W._Byrd","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_W._Byrd?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_W._Byrd?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:James_W._Byrd"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_W._Byrd","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/James_W._Byrd","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_W._Byrd?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:James_W._Byrd"}},"extract":"James W. Byrd is an American politician and former Democratic member of the Wyoming House of Representatives, representing the 44th district from 2009 to 2019. Byrd retired from his House of Representatives seat to run for Wyoming Secretary of State shortly after Republican incumbent Ed Murray resigned, but lost the November 2018 election to Murray's successor Edward Buchanan.","extract_html":"<p><b>James W. Byrd</b> is an American politician and former Democratic member of the Wyoming House of Representatives, representing the 44th district from 2009 to 2019. Byrd retired from his House of Representatives seat to run for Wyoming Secretary of State shortly after Republican incumbent Ed Murray resigned, but lost the November 2018 election to Murray's successor Edward Buchanan.</p>"}